sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-bauhinia-variegata-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bauhinia-variegata-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bauhinia-variegata-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bauhinia variegata Turing wavenumber at 69.12 µm (Pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 78.9/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 implements Schnakenberg kinetics and the Turing wavenumber on a periodic patch sized so the linear wavelength is 69.12 µm (6.912e-05 m, log10 = -4.160), age 0 Ma. The equal-diffusion control is stable (sigma_max = -0.1) and a single-mode integration recovers sigma(k_c) (0.193 versus 0.188). The first adult frame pasted an opaque inset over the photograph and the grayscale Pearson r was 0.9776. The diffusion-ratio sweep barely moved lambda. The 1 cm bar was not yet measured, so the sampling limit was missing. Those three gaps are the remediation list. Overall 78.9/100 (faithfulness 77.0, reproducibility 83.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 68, Morphometric validation 72, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 82. Output judged: docs/media/bauhinia_variegata_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-bauhinia-variegata-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 485676 B, 1512×1008 px, artifact_sha256 5a38587e481dd1f33401575320542b13e2b3ddc508ba12df428a1454b16c15b9 (sha256 5a38587e481dd1f33401575320542b13e2b3ddc508ba12df428a1454b16c15b9), spec_fingerprint 68eb58e3e0bb1a60ce52a1d3e30e4b90290cf6fbeabcbc36606d815cdc1da28e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 68eb58e3e0bb1a60ce52a1d3e30e4b90290cf6fbeabcbc36606d815cdc1da28e; artifact_sha256: 5a38587e481dd1f33401575320542b13e2b3ddc508ba12df428a1454b16c15b9; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/bauhinia_variegata_turing_wavelength_s0/bauhinia_variegata_specimen.jpg=300694d305567ca5..., datasets/bauhinia_variegata_turing_wavelength_s0/bauhinia_variegata_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=65eb5aab368642b9...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a finite wavenumber when inhibitor diffusion is fast enough. Schnakenberg (1979) supplies the trimolecular kinetics. Kondo & Miura (2010) review wavelength selection by reaction and diffusion rates. | Armon et al. (2011) measured centimetre-scale helical opening of Bauhinia variegata valves. That is a different law.; reconstructed_in_script: D_u and D_v are chosen so the linear k_c equals 2π/69.12 µm. The 69.12 µm length is the assigned detail scale of this slot, not a counted spacing on the pericarp.; transfer_boundary: The photograph is a centimetre-scale herbarium scan (CC BY-SA 3.0, Roger Culos). It shows the valve envelope. It does not resolve 69.12 µm.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a published 69.12 µm pigment measurement for Bauhinia variegata. | Does not claim the reaction-diffusion field generates the pod silhouette or the seed positions. | Does not reuse Armon et al. curvature parameters.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Blend the adult inset into the photograph and quantise the GIF from the adult frame's palette so full-frame Pearson r exceeds 0.98.",
            "remediation needed: Keep the equal-diffusion ablation, and put its dispersion curve on the comparison figure next to the unstable band.",
            "remediation needed: Measure the printed 1 cm bar and report 69.12 µm in pixels. Segment the valve and report a valve-masked KS separate from the paper-white KS.",
            "remediation needed: Replace the diffusion-ratio sweep with a diffusivity-scale sweep. Lambda must move as sqrt(D), which is the parameter that sets the wavelength." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.789"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

